fter the `if` statement is evaluated.\n- **Execution Path Analysis:** The execution flow of `svp_simple_698_001_main` will always reach line 27.\n- **Conclusion:** The read operation on line 27 is **executable**.\n\n### Final Report Generation\n\nAll three operations involved in the reported atomicity violation are executable. A possible interleaving demonstrating the violation is as follows:\n1. `main` starts. `__VERIFIER_nondet_int()` returns a non-zero value for `r`.\n2. The condition `if (r)` on line 22 is true.\n3. `main` executes `g = 17;` on line 23.\n4. An interrupt occurs, preempting `main`. `svp_simple_698_001_isr_1` is executed.\n5. The ISR executes `g = 42;` on line 13.\n6. The ISR finishes, and control returns to `main`.\n7. `main` executes `t = g;` on line 27, reading the value 42, which was written by the ISR.\n\nThis sequence matches the reported `['Write', 'Write', 'Read']` pattern across lines [23, 13, 27]. The violation is valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"23\", \"13\", \"27\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
